{
  "baseline": "6fce2e641760b8eff62adad512f4096fb1502fed",
  "scope": "Registered definitions at baseline. v3 adapters preserve current Policy and original domain authorities. adapted means local mechanism coverage, never per-domain end-to-end acceptance. Scheduled receipt background continuation reuses the original Actor queue/context. ERP direct completion admitted for erp.item.tag.add; exact title-only item.general.addorupdate may complete after a later native item.single.get postcondition with exact session or persisted provider-observed refresh lineage, locally verified. Other fields/methods/async finality remain unverified. File restore now binds original backups and no-clobber publication to native journal/atomic deleted_files settlement; file deletion now has per-item backup/settlement and guarded original-version remaining-item resume through the original ToolRuntime/Policy/confirmation and real native invocation ledger, locally verified. v3 generate_video now has native async queue, original ledger, single-submit uncertainty, owned asset publication and original Actor continuation, locally verified without external calls. 362 adds authenticated read-only user-chat progress and persisted discovery markers, locally verified through HTTP/message/frontend paths; accepted/uncertain is never delivery completion. 363 persists authenticated in-flight Actor steer with atomic checkpoint/ACK and same-root continuation delivery; delivery does not amend requirements or authorize new effects. 364/365 add in-flight STEER relation review, host-verified requirement revisions preserving all prior artifacts/results/operations/context, versioned planning gates and native dispatch barriers, locally verified only. Original two pinned method protocols are compared without creating Skills or calling providers. 366/367 add same-conversation personal serial new-user-turn adoption with original checkpoint/context/pins and requirement review, plus exact canonical generate_image reuse of authorized published historical images before charging; locally verified only. Late native images settle through original Actor consumers. 368 adds shared native preparation for exact ready-plan and final-prompt reuse, and committed structured task-plan handoff with fresh fact review. Stable regeneration retries reuse only matching source/variant descendants; explicit unkeyed regeneration keeps new-image semantics. Original two published body hashes match repository v3 and complete local control flows; production full export, provider and UI acceptance are still unverified. Channel progress, remaining ERP terminal contracts, multi-entry/visual UI, original two-Skill live acceptance and whole-product acceptance remain incomplete. 369 persists bounded/redacted native ERP mapped-request evidence and exposes partial item observations/provider handles after compression. Lost ACK target-state observations never complete unknown effects or unblock conflicting mutations. Method-specific batch/async terminal contracts and wakeups remain pending; no external calls. 370 adds exact acknowledged product string-field postconditions (title plus barcode/unit/remark/shortTitle) using existing item.single.get, original input/mapped equality and separate versioned read projection. Unknown and async/partial remain unresolved; no SKU/inventory/pricing coercion. Locally verified only. 371 adds original-message pause/resume/cancel UI with source-preserving logical resume, native scoped HTTP controls and local browser acceptance (fixture API/images only); completed roots are rechecked for authenticated follow-ups. Accepted ERP writes project as needs_verification rather than guaranteed pending delivery. A current 88-write method inventory identifies 2 conditional verification protocols and 86 methods needing provider-specific finality; discovery never grants completion or resend authority. Channel-specific progress and original two-Skill provider acceptance remain pending. 372 user explicitly defers new ERP write adaptation and retains original ERP Agent. Earlier 86-method finality gaps are deferred rather than completed. New-task admission is restricted to supported personal workspace scopes; existing channel Actor/Skill paths and saved bootstrap/state recovery are preserved. Current release_scope overrides earlier pending scope notes. 373 enforces deferred ERP scope in code with an independent default-false new-effect gate across planning/disclosure/dispatch/native preparation. Original ERP Agent and old effect recovery remain; non-ERP shared lifecycle and context/reuse paths locally verified. Real original-Skill availability/export/provider acceptance remains unverified.",
